# ── Data sources (the two platforms are completely separate) ────────────────
# FREE TRIAL platform  → embedded Postgres (PGlite), seeded from
#                        supabase/seed-trial.sql. Needs no configuration and
#                        never reads DATABASE_URL.
# FULL platform        → hosted Postgres over DATABASE_URL. Never falls back
#                        to the trial's embedded database; when DATABASE_URL
#                        is unset the /welcome picker disables it and says so.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dbname
#
# Optional: PGSSL=disable to turn off TLS (local Postgres); PGPOOL_MAX=5 pool size.
# Optional: PGLITE_DATA_DIR to move the trial's data directory, or set it to
#           "memory" to force an in-memory trial database. On Vercel / Lambda
#           the filesystem is read-only, so the trial runs in memory
#           automatically and resets on each cold start.

# ── Platform (which product this build ships) ──────────────────────────────
# SPIR_PLATFORM selects which platform is compiled in.
#   (unset) — GENERAL build: both platforms compiled in and the /welcome
#             picker chooses per visitor. This is the deployment default.
#   local   — trial installer only: embedded PGlite, no sign-in at all.
#   cloud   — full product only: hosted Postgres, fixed admin sign-in.
#             Requires DATABASE_URL.
# Use `npm run build:local` / `npm run build:cloud` for the dedicated builds;
# a plain `npm run build` produces the general one.
# SPIR_PLATFORM=local

# ── Auth ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Session-signing secret. REQUIRED for any real deployment (a hosted DB or
# platform): without it, sessions are signed with a public built-in key and can
# be forged, and the app refuses to start. Generate one, e.g.:
#   openssl rand -base64 48
# AUTH_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-value
